# Translation workflow

## Default target
- locale: zh-Hant
- aliases: Traditional Chinese, 繁體中文
- source: zh (Simplified Chinese UI dictionaries; Chinese-first key set)

## Surfaces
- in scope: product UI locale dictionaries registered through `ctx.locale.register` (`zh` / `en` / `zh-Hant`)
- out of scope: documentation pairing (`.md` / `.zh.md` / `.i18n.yaml`), VitePress, AGENTS.md, comments, JSDoc, logging

## Include
- `packages/**/src/**/locales.ts`
- `packages/**/src/**/locales/*.ts`
- inline `ctx.locale.register(...)` dictionary objects in client plugins

## Exclude
- `*.md`
- `*.zh.md`
- `*.i18n.yaml`
- `docs/**`
- `website/**`
- `**/AGENTS.md`
- comments and JSDoc

## Missing detection
- Typed `register(ns, dicts)` requires `Record<LocaleId, LocaleDictOf<N>>`; a missing `zh-Hant` seat or missing key is a compile error (`satisfies Record<Key, string>` / `Record<Key, string>`).
- Untyped namespaces must register a matching `zh-Hant` dictionary in the same effect as `zh` and `en`.
- After a merge, scan the git range for `locale.register` calls and `export const zh` dictionaries that lack a `zh-Hant` counterpart.

## Process
- Keep `zh` as the key-set source of truth.
- Add a complete `zhHant` dictionary next to `zh`/`en` and pass `'zh-Hant': zhHant` in the same typed `register` call.
- Translate from the Simplified `zh` copy. Do not use runtime OpenCC or treat conversion output as source of truth.
- Do not add Traditional Chinese documentation or site locales.

## Verify
- `pnpm exec vitest run` on the owning package's client specs (dictionary occupancy and `setLocale('zh-Hant')` copy)
- Typecheck of the edited packages (typed `register` / `satisfies`)

## Style
- comments/JSDoc/logging: English
- user-facing: zh-Hant
- terminology: none (align product terms with the Simplified `zh` dictionary)
